  "title": "Erdős Problem #892",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Is there a necessary and sufficient condition for a sequence of integers $b_1<b_2<\\cdots$ that ensures there exists a primitive sequence $a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ (i.e. no element divides another) with $a_n \\ll b_n$ for all $n$?\nIn particular, is this always possible if there are no non-trivial solutions to $(b_i,b_j)=b_k$?",
